        "last_commit_message": "feat(llm): extra request-body fields via LLM_EXTRA_BODY (#1495)\n\n* feat(llm): extra request-body fields via LLM_EXTRA_BODY\n\nSome provider parameters, such as OpenAI's service_tier and\nsafety_identifier, are read only from the request body, so\nLLM_EXTRA_HEADERS can't set them. LLM_EXTRA_BODY merges a JSON object\ninto the body of every request to the configured model, on both routing\npaths. A dedicated dedupe model gets its own DEDUPE_LLM_EXTRA_BODY\ninstead, as with headers.\n\n* fix(config): decode saved JSON-object settings when loading\n\npersist_current() saves env values verbatim, so LLM_EXTRA_HEADERS,\nLLM_EXTRA_BODY and their DEDUPE_ variants land in cli-config.json as JSON\ntext. The loader passed that text unchanged to the dict fields, so a later\nlaunch without the env var failed validation. Decode saved strings for\ndict fields, as pydantic-settings does for env vars.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Szymon Nastaly <szymon.nastaly@autoform.ch>",
